00:23:56,803 --> 00:23:58,538
Wakka-chukka-boom.
Chukka-wakka-chukka boom.

506
00:23:58,572 --> 00:24:01,307
Tell your boss,
I can't afford to fool around.

507
00:24:01,340 --> 00:24:02,442
His time is up.

508
00:24:02,475 --> 00:24:04,043
He don't feel that way.

509
00:24:16,022 --> 00:24:17,890
♪♪ [Humming]

510
00:24:17,923 --> 00:24:20,660
You know, dolphins are really
smart, aren't they?

511
00:24:20,693 --> 00:24:22,562
Oh, yeah, totally.
Smart as you please.

512
00:24:22,595 --> 00:24:24,030
Oh, yeah, the way they
jump for things.

513
00:24:24,063 --> 00:24:26,600
- Yeah.
- And click and buzz
to kind of talk,

514
00:24:26,633 --> 00:24:28,402
flip over and...

515
00:24:28,435 --> 00:24:29,937
Swim.
There's that.

516
00:24:29,970 --> 00:24:31,872
And eat fish.

517
00:24:31,905 --> 00:24:33,973
- Yeah.
- Other things, I guess.

518
00:24:34,007 --> 00:24:36,910
You know, dolphins are really
dumb, aren't they?

519
00:24:36,943 --> 00:24:38,445
Hell, I don't know anymore.

520
00:24:38,478 --> 00:24:40,080
What's with dolphins anyways,
you guys?

521
00:24:40,113 --> 00:24:41,582
Are they smart
or are they dumb?

522
00:24:41,615 --> 00:24:42,948
Well, let's find out.

523
00:24:42,982 --> 00:24:44,852
I have seaworld
on my speed dial.

524
00:24:44,885 --> 00:24:46,485
Let's just call them and see.

525
00:24:46,520 --> 00:24:48,455
[Dialing, ringing]

526
00:24:48,488 --> 00:24:49,422
[Man]
It's a great day at seaworld.

527
00:24:49,455 --> 00:24:50,457
How may I direct your call?

528
00:24:50,490 --> 00:24:52,958
Hi, yeah, blowy the dolphin,
please.

529
00:24:52,992 --> 00:24:54,527
I'll connect you.

530
00:24:54,560 --> 00:24:55,528
Blowy?

531
00:24:55,562 --> 00:24:56,530
Yeah, there's always a blowy.

532
00:24:56,563 --> 00:24:57,797
[Dolphin clicks]

533
00:24:57,830 --> 00:24:59,665
Hi, blowy?
Mike nelson here.

534
00:24:59,698 --> 00:25:02,068
See, we have a rather delicate
question for you.

535
00:25:02,102 --> 00:25:03,603
[Clicking]

536
00:25:03,637 --> 00:25:06,607
So are you guys just stupid
or what's going on anyway?

537
00:25:06,640 --> 00:25:07,840
[Squeaking]

538
00:25:07,873 --> 00:25:09,475
Yeah, I mean,
if you're so smart,

539
00:25:09,508 --> 00:25:11,812
how come you don't speak
english or play the drums?

540
00:25:11,845 --> 00:25:13,112
[Squeaking]

541
00:25:13,145 --> 00:25:14,613
Yeah...
[Squeaking]

542
00:25:14,647 --> 00:25:16,583
That's your answer
to everything, pal.

543
00:25:16,617 --> 00:25:17,583
- Well, listen up, flipper.
- Blowy.

544
00:25:17,617 --> 00:25:19,618
Yeah, blowy, whatever.

545
00:25:19,685 --> 00:25:21,655
Everyone thinks you're
einstein or something.

546
00:25:21,688 --> 00:25:23,557
We think you're just an
evolutionary cul-de-sac,

547
00:25:23,590 --> 00:25:25,125
couldn't swim your way
out of a hot tub.

548
00:25:25,158 --> 00:25:26,158
What do you think
of them sardines?

549
00:25:26,192 --> 00:25:27,893
[Squeaking]

550
00:25:27,927 --> 00:25:29,195
Oh, yeah.

551
00:25:29,228 --> 00:25:30,630
Hey, tell it to fa, pal.

552
00:25:30,663 --> 00:25:32,032
Or better yet,
why don't you talk to me?

553
00:25:32,065 --> 00:25:34,167
Come on up here.
Let your flippers
do the talking

554
00:25:34,200 --> 00:25:35,668
because I am standing here,
man.

555
00:25:35,702 --> 00:25:36,637
I'm waiting for you.

556
00:25:36,670 --> 00:25:37,837
Come on.
Bring it on.

557
00:25:37,870 --> 00:25:41,775
[Laser pulses]

558
00:25:41,775 --> 00:25:43,610
Alarm. A dolphin war ship

559
00:25:43,643 --> 00:25:46,680
has just de-cloaked
off the port bow.

560
00:25:46,713 --> 00:25:48,548
Cambot, get me
rocket number nine.

561
00:25:51,283 --> 00:25:53,620
Its propulsion
and weapons systems

562
00:25:53,653 --> 00:25:56,555
are advanced far beyond
our understanding.

563
00:25:56,590 --> 00:25:58,958
[Whimpering]

564
00:25:58,992 --> 00:26:02,695
[Dolphin squeaking]

565
00:26:04,197 --> 00:26:05,698
Hi, uh, blowy?

566
00:26:05,732 --> 00:26:06,933
We're sorry about everything.

567
00:26:06,967 --> 00:26:08,768
Yeah, we didn't understand.

568
00:26:08,802 --> 00:26:10,303
So, again, sorry.

569
00:26:10,337 --> 00:26:11,303
Take it all back.

570
00:26:11,337 --> 00:26:14,975
Sorry. Sorry about that.
Bye.

571
00:26:15,008 --> 00:26:16,042
[Sighs]

572
00:26:16,075 --> 00:26:18,278
You know, dolphins
are really smart.

573
00:26:18,312 --> 00:26:22,315
- Sure are.
- Yeah, really smart,
but touchy.

574
00:26:22,348 --> 00:26:23,850
Be right back.

575
00:26:23,883 --> 00:26:26,052
Man, say the slightest thing.

576
00:26:34,360 --> 00:26:35,362
There, it's fixed.

577
00:26:38,230 --> 00:26:41,367
- Hey!
- Stop in the name of europe.

578
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:42,735
What the hell are you doing?

579
00:26:42,768 --> 00:26:44,870
It's a middleton group
of tube-amp lovers.

580
00:26:48,908 --> 00:26:51,477
Kick, punch,
it's all in the mind.

581
00:26:52,812 --> 00:26:55,248
He's enjoying the bold,
adventurous life

582
00:26:55,282 --> 00:26:57,817
of a tv repairman.

583
00:27:00,053 --> 00:27:01,955
You bastard lou reed.

584
00:27:01,988 --> 00:27:03,590
Let's go.

585
00:27:03,623 --> 00:27:05,658
Stay. I'll put coffee on.

586
00:27:05,692 --> 00:27:11,430
[Sandra]
Peter! Peter!

587
00:27:11,463 --> 00:27:12,332
I'm over here.

588
00:27:12,365 --> 00:27:15,368
♪ Over here, over here ♪

589
00:27:15,402 --> 00:27:17,303
Oh, my god, peter.

590
00:27:17,337 --> 00:27:19,272
Is-a your penis okay?

591
00:27:19,305 --> 00:27:21,040
What happened?

592
00:27:21,073 --> 00:27:22,642
They smashed the converter.

593
00:27:22,675 --> 00:27:23,777
You work all night,

594
00:27:23,810 --> 00:27:25,345
and they come and smash it
to bits.

595
00:27:25,378 --> 00:27:27,580
Do you think you could
identify them?

596
00:27:27,613 --> 00:27:31,450
No. They were only interested
in that damn converter.

597
00:27:31,483 --> 00:27:32,852
Smashed it to bits.

598
00:27:33,920 --> 00:27:36,890
Oh, hey, mr. Food,
the fishing guy.

599
00:27:36,923 --> 00:27:38,992
Whoops.

600
00:27:39,025 --> 00:27:43,328
♪♪ [Soft strings]

601
00:27:43,363 --> 00:27:46,432
Sounds like they're in search
of the mysterious underwater
yanni caves.

602
00:27:51,470 --> 00:27:54,473
He's getting paid 10 large
to whack a grouper.

603
00:28:00,647 --> 00:28:04,983
I just ate harvey mackay.

604
00:28:05,017 --> 00:28:06,953
You know, you shoot scuba
diving in slow motion,

605
00:28:06,987 --> 00:28:08,855
you could actually go
back in time.

606
00:28:16,695 --> 00:28:19,498
A human!
We've got to clear the oceans.

607
00:28:21,868 --> 00:28:23,903
Oh, no, there's that shark
that asked me out.

608
00:28:26,138 --> 00:28:27,540
Shark!

609
00:28:27,573 --> 00:28:30,643
Help! Shark!

610
00:28:30,677 --> 00:28:32,678
Give me a hand!

611
00:28:32,712 --> 00:28:33,913
It's going away.

612
00:28:33,947 --> 00:28:36,148
My rash-- it's going away.

613
00:28:36,182 --> 00:28:40,887
It's going away.
It's going away.

614
00:28:40,920 --> 00:28:42,955
I'm made of ground chalk
and lava.

615
00:28:44,623 --> 00:28:46,625
[Slow motion]
Slow day, hun?

616
00:28:51,497 --> 00:28:53,533
- Let's get out of here.
- Yeah, yeah.

617
00:28:55,135 --> 00:28:57,103
Florinda was
one of my associates,

618
00:28:57,137 --> 00:28:58,705
one of the best.

619
00:28:58,738 --> 00:29:00,540
Uh, associates,
as I mentioned.

620
00:29:00,573 --> 00:29:02,075
Her death will be
a serious loss to us.

621
00:29:02,108 --> 00:29:04,510
Boy, could she type
and light file.

622
00:29:04,543 --> 00:29:07,747
I must say she wasn't feeling
any too well lately.

623
00:29:07,780 --> 00:29:10,082
Do you think it was
an accident,

624
00:29:10,117 --> 00:29:12,985
or could she have
committed suicide?

625
00:29:13,018 --> 00:29:14,520
Huh?

626
00:29:14,553 --> 00:29:16,088
I think that's up to you
to decide.

627
00:29:16,122 --> 00:29:17,523
Yeah, right on.

628
00:29:17,557 --> 00:29:18,958
Well, we did accident yesterday.

629
00:29:18,992 --> 00:29:20,092
That was kind of boring.

630
00:29:20,127 --> 00:29:21,560
I think I'll decide on murder.

631
00:29:21,593 --> 00:29:22,562
What the hell?

632
00:29:22,595 --> 00:29:24,463
You know if she had
any enemies?

633
00:29:24,497 --> 00:29:26,232
No, absolutely not.

634
00:29:26,265 --> 00:29:29,102
When was the last time
you saw her?

635
00:29:29,135 --> 00:29:31,170
Yesterday.

636
00:29:31,203 --> 00:29:33,238
In the morning,
when she left the lab.

637
00:29:33,272 --> 00:29:36,943
And so none of you knew
she was going on a trip.

638
00:29:36,977 --> 00:29:38,945
- She had just packed her bags--
- sheriff.

639
00:29:39,012 --> 00:29:43,650
Here at the w.O.I.
We don't poke into people's
private affairs.

640
00:29:43,683 --> 00:29:44,850
All we know about florinda

641
00:29:44,883 --> 00:29:46,987
is that she was
an excellent researcher.

642
00:29:47,020 --> 00:29:50,122
What specific research
did florinda do?

643
00:29:50,157 --> 00:29:54,593
She was working on the
properties of ribonucleic acid.

644
00:29:54,627 --> 00:29:57,497
That's a substance necessary
to life.

645
00:29:57,530 --> 00:29:59,965
Like cigarettes, fire,
and thumbs.

646
00:30:04,670 --> 00:30:06,538
Come on.
Let's see what you can do.

647
00:30:06,572 --> 00:30:08,908
Well, this is about it.
I hate to disappoint you.

648
00:30:08,942 --> 00:30:11,010
Hey, slow down!

649
00:30:11,043 --> 00:30:16,015
Come back here.
Where you going?

650
00:30:16,048 --> 00:30:17,617
[Gasps]

651
00:30:17,650 --> 00:30:20,052
Fluffy, bad dog.

652
00:30:24,023 --> 00:30:26,692
Open to downtown shackville.

653
00:30:31,797 --> 00:30:35,568
Hey, rob reiner.

654
00:30:35,602 --> 00:30:38,003
Hurry up.
Our shift's almost over.

655
00:30:41,307 --> 00:30:43,577
This guy just fell asleep, sir.

656
00:30:49,182 --> 00:30:51,717
It's hard to believe, sheriff.

657
00:30:51,750 --> 00:30:52,852
- Cortez?
- Yes, sir.

658
00:30:52,885 --> 00:30:55,222
I want a cast
made of that wound.

659
00:30:55,255 --> 00:30:56,788
- Go on.
- Yes, sir.

660
00:30:56,822 --> 00:30:58,825
Good thing yoko's there.

661
00:30:58,858 --> 00:31:00,593
[Groaning]

662
00:31:00,627 --> 00:31:04,330
I can't believe I directed
north.

663
00:31:04,363 --> 00:31:09,102
Can't believe I got sent
to the principal's office again.

664
00:31:09,135 --> 00:31:10,403
Well, doc?

665
00:31:10,437 --> 00:31:12,338
We're saving him,
but he's still in shock.

666
00:31:12,372 --> 00:31:13,973
Any chance of interrogating--

667
00:31:14,007 --> 00:31:15,040
[woman]
Doctor, hurry!

668
00:31:15,073 --> 00:31:16,742
- Hardly.
- What's wrong?

669
00:31:16,775 --> 00:31:19,812
- Another crisis.
- The nurse needs
making out with.

670
00:31:20,947 --> 00:31:22,782
- The sedative.
- Yes.

671
00:31:24,983 --> 00:31:27,053
Here you go.
This'll make your coat shiny.

672
00:31:30,022 --> 00:31:31,657
[Doctor]
That should do it.
Stay with him.

673
00:31:31,690 --> 00:31:33,358
Yes, doctor.

674
00:31:33,392 --> 00:31:34,993
May I come in, please?

675
00:31:38,263 --> 00:31:39,665
We might get some information

676
00:31:39,698 --> 00:31:42,068
form the cast taken
of his friend's arm.

677
00:31:42,102 --> 00:31:43,268
I examined the body carefully,

678
00:31:43,302 --> 00:31:45,070
and I can say without a doubt

679
00:31:45,103 --> 00:31:48,140
they were both attacked
by the same animal,
the same shark.

680
00:31:48,140 --> 00:31:53,078
Another dark-shaded,
mobbed-up doctor.

681
00:31:53,112 --> 00:31:57,083
Whatever it is, I think it's
good we took it out of him.

682
00:31:57,117 --> 00:31:59,518
Good morning, doctor.

683
00:31:59,552 --> 00:32:01,520
My god, what the hell is that?

684
00:32:01,553 --> 00:32:04,357
Whatever it is, I wouldn't want
to rub it the wrong way.

685
00:32:04,390 --> 00:32:06,425
Well, I would.

686
00:32:06,458 --> 00:32:08,995
- I'm not an expert...
- But this is pointy.

687
00:32:09,028 --> 00:32:12,098
...but these don't look like
the teeth marks
of a shark to me.

688
00:32:12,132 --> 00:32:15,435
What else you think
it might be then?

689
00:32:15,468 --> 00:32:17,737
I'll answer that as soon as we
cut back to our scene.

690
00:32:17,770 --> 00:32:19,172
It shouldn't be long.

691
00:32:19,205 --> 00:32:20,005
Try it now.

692
00:32:21,140 --> 00:32:23,308
I get nothing.
Nothing.

693
00:32:23,342 --> 00:32:25,043
No respect.

694
00:32:25,077 --> 00:32:27,247
What do you mean nothing?
Did you put the fuse in?

695
00:32:29,248 --> 00:32:31,217
Of course I inserted
the damn fuse.

696
00:32:31,283 --> 00:32:32,552
What do you take me for?

697
00:32:32,585 --> 00:32:34,220
No comment.

698
00:32:34,253 --> 00:32:36,722
Oh, he threw
a little euro-tantrum.

699
00:32:36,755 --> 00:32:38,658
They've been going on
like that all morning.

700
00:32:38,692 --> 00:32:40,793
Geniuses should never
work together.

701
00:32:40,827 --> 00:32:44,230
But these two guys'll be fine.

702
00:32:44,263 --> 00:32:47,067
Sandra. Sandra.

703
00:32:47,100 --> 00:32:49,135
Yes, master?

704
00:32:49,168 --> 00:32:51,403
Don't be a wise...
And go see what's wrong
with the monitor.

705
00:32:51,437 --> 00:32:54,740
Yeah.

706
00:32:54,773 --> 00:32:56,708
I want to come up here
and pout a little bit.

707
00:32:56,742 --> 00:32:59,345
Is that okay
if I pout a little?

708
00:32:59,378 --> 00:33:01,447
Think it'll work?

709
00:33:01,480 --> 00:33:03,415
What, are you kidding?

710
00:33:03,448 --> 00:33:05,117
I like the color of your eyes.

711
00:33:05,150 --> 00:33:06,552
The rest of you is hideous.

712
00:33:06,585 --> 00:33:09,488
Bye.

713
00:33:12,692 --> 00:33:15,795
Okay, genius, we're getting
a signal here.

714
00:33:15,828 --> 00:33:17,797
Finally. I'm going below.
Stay tuned.

715
00:33:17,830 --> 00:33:19,232
All right.

716
00:33:19,265 --> 00:33:20,867
[Foreign accent]
Boy, am I from florida.

717
00:33:24,503 --> 00:33:28,140
Isn't that one guy's
eye color gross?

718
00:33:28,173 --> 00:33:29,508
When will he be ready?

719
00:33:29,542 --> 00:33:33,512
Just a couple more hours.

720
00:33:33,545 --> 00:33:35,748
I'm going back to italy.
Bye.

721
00:33:40,787 --> 00:33:42,488
Kiss my ink sac.

722
00:33:45,758 --> 00:33:47,927
♪♪ [Hums "sailor's hornpipe"]

723
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:49,228
Crap.

724
00:33:50,295 --> 00:33:52,732
I'm sorry about your vacation.

725
00:33:52,765 --> 00:33:54,333
Oh, really?

726
00:33:54,367 --> 00:33:59,238
Oh, no, he suspects my
insincerity about his vacation.

727
00:33:59,272 --> 00:34:02,308
So far I like these scenes
the best.

728
00:34:05,343 --> 00:34:07,913
I was going to say how sorry
I was about your cat dying,

729
00:34:07,947 --> 00:34:09,515
but forget it.

730
00:34:09,548 --> 00:34:11,683
[Beeping]

731
00:34:11,717 --> 00:34:14,553
Oh, I forgot to lick
the beer off the can.

732
00:34:14,587 --> 00:34:16,422
[Electronic sound]

733
00:34:16,455 --> 00:34:17,823
What's that?

734
00:34:17,857 --> 00:34:20,358
- Kraftwerk.
- Not sure.

735
00:34:20,392 --> 00:34:22,762
Hang on a second.

736
00:34:22,795 --> 00:34:25,363
- Wait.
- Hold on. Wait. Pause.

737
00:34:25,397 --> 00:34:26,765
Okay, we got it.

738
00:34:26,798 --> 00:34:28,333
A shark?

739
00:34:28,367 --> 00:34:29,702
You think it's him?

740
00:34:29,735 --> 00:34:31,337
I don't know.
Might be.

741
00:34:31,370 --> 00:34:33,005
It's moving fast,

742
00:34:33,038 --> 00:34:34,373
almost 30 knots.

743
00:34:35,842 --> 00:34:38,443
Judging from the sound
of its echo,

744
00:34:38,477 --> 00:34:41,447
displaces a tremendous
amount of water for a fish.

745
00:34:41,513 --> 00:34:42,815
Do you read anything else?

746
00:34:45,350 --> 00:34:48,453
I don't know.
Must've dived too deep.

747
00:34:48,487 --> 00:34:50,557
Yeah, to say the least.

748
00:34:50,590 --> 00:34:53,025
Maybe it wasn't him.

749
00:34:53,058 --> 00:34:55,260
Hey, bob, save us a beer, too.
Huh?

750
00:34:55,293 --> 00:34:56,762
I was framed, I tell ya.

751
00:34:56,795 --> 00:34:58,697
You want another?
Then find that fish.

752
00:34:58,730 --> 00:35:00,165
That's euro-funny.

753
00:35:05,070 --> 00:35:08,007
Now, how do these fit?

754
00:35:08,040 --> 00:35:09,475
You did a good job.

755
00:35:09,508 --> 00:35:11,043
Buy yourself something ugly.

756
00:35:11,077 --> 00:35:12,077
Need anything else?

757
00:35:12,110 --> 00:35:13,412
Just keep an eye on him.

758
00:35:13,445 --> 00:35:16,315
I'll let you know
when we need something else.

759
00:35:25,057 --> 00:35:27,025
Man, jet skis
are getting huge.

760
00:35:29,128 --> 00:35:30,930
I was only 19 when I met bob.

761
00:35:30,963 --> 00:35:32,265
That's when I was skinny.

762
00:35:32,298 --> 00:35:34,133
He was with the english
